2d:["$","ul","2",{"className":"Legal-module__2dCIza__list","children":[["$","li","You. You send a prompt, and optionally attached files, images or video, from the Keplar app.",{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"You."}]," ","You send a prompt, and optionally attached files, images or video, from the Keplar app."]}],["$","li","Keplar. Keplar-One classifies the request and decides which models are needed. Simple questions may go to one model; complex ones go to several.",{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Keplar."}]," ","Keplar-One classifies the request and decides which models are needed. Simple questions may go to one model; complex ones go to several."]}],["$","li","Selected model providers. Only the providers chosen for that request receive what they need to answer it: your prompt, the recent conversation for context, any attached content, and (if memory is on) a few short notes about you that are relevant to the question. On Free, saved notes and the text of attached documents are not part of that.",{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Selected model providers."}]," ","Only the providers chosen for that request receive what they need to answer it: your prompt, the recent conversation for context, any attached content, and (if memory is on) a few short notes about you that are relevant to the question. On Free, saved notes and the text of attached documents are not part of that."]}],["$","li","Keplar-One synthesis. Keplar compares the responses, weighs the reasoning behind each, looks into disagreements and writes one answer.",{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Keplar-One synthesis."}]," ","Keplar compares the responses, weighs the reasoning behind each, looks into disagreements and writes one answer."]}],["$","li","You. You receive the answer along with its consensus, the models consulted, any sources the models cited and disagreements.",{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"You."}]," ","You receive the answer along with its consensus, the models consulted, any sources the models cited and disagreements."]}]]}]
2e:["$","p","3",{"className":"Legal-module__2dCIza__p","children":"Your account email and name are not sent to model providers."}]
30:[["$","strong",null,{"children":"App data in your browser."}]," ","Your chats while signed out, your settings, your \"what will you use Keplar for\" choice and upgrade-note dismissals, in local storage on your device."]
46:T491,Analytics (optional, off by default). If you choose Accept all or turn on Analytics, the public marketing pages (not the app) load Vercel Web Analytics and Speed Insights. They count page views, button clicks and page speed without cookies and without following you across sites. Events carry the page, the button's placement and campaign tags, never your questions, email or account details. With Analytics on, Keplar also records in its own database which public page a visit started on, a coarse source type (for example search, social or direct), campaign tags, and whether that same browser later signed up, asked a question or received an answer. It uses a random identifier kept on your device, with no link to your account, and never records your questions, files, email, IP address or the address of the page you came from. These records are deleted after 180 days, and browsers that send Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track are left out. If you reject them, no analytics script is loaded and no events are sent. Change your choice any time with Cookie settings in the site footer or on your Account page; scripts already loaded stop on your next page load.31:["$","p","2",{"className":"Legal-module__2dCIza__p","children":"$46"}]
32:["$","p","3",{"className":"Legal-module__2dCIza__p","children":"Ad measurement (Whop Pixel). Keplar uses the Whop Pixel, a script from Whop, to measure how its own advertising performs. It loads on the public marketing pages only: not in the app, on your account, in checkout, or on sign-in, sign-up, contact and other form pages. It records page views, so Whop learns which page was opened, the page you came from, your browser, device, language and time zone, and a random identifier it keeps in a first-party cookie and local storage on keplar.one. Keplar has turned off the pixel's automatic capture of email, phone and name entries, and sends it nothing else: not your questions, files, email or account details. Whop uses this to link visits to ad clicks and purchases, under its own privacy policy."}]
33:["$","p","4",{"className":"Legal-module__2dCIza__p","children":"Who is on the site right now (no cookies, always on). While a Keplar page is open and visible in your browser, it sends a small signal about every 15 seconds, and one more when you close or leave the page. The server keeps only the same kind of anonymous daily code described below and the time of the last signal, and treats the code as present for about 40 seconds after it. It stores no IP address, no page, no referrer, no account and no cookie, and it deletes the entry when you leave and clears old ones within minutes. The signal does not start until the page has finished loading and the browser is idle, it pauses when the tab is hidden, and it is never sent from admin pages, for Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control, or by bots. Only the Keplar team sees the resulting count."}]
34:["$","p","5",{"className":"Legal-module__2dCIza__p","children":"Visit counts (no cookies, always on). Keplar counts visits to its own pages on its server so we know roughly how many people use it. It stores a daily anonymous code made from your IP address and browser details plus a secret, so the code cannot be linked across days or turned back into your IP address, and the IP address and browser details themselves are never stored. We keep the code, the day, the first part of the page path (for example /pricing), and the website you came from (the site name only, never the full address). We do not count bots, prefetches, or visits that send Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control. Only the Keplar team sees the totals. Per-visit rows are rolled up into daily totals after 35 days."}]
35:["$","p","6",{"className":"Legal-module__2dCIza__p","children":"Checkout. When you open checkout to buy a plan, the payment form is loaded from Whop, our payment processor, and Whop handles your card details and its own cookies. It loads only because you asked to pay."}]
36:["$","p","7",{"className":"Legal-module__2dCIza__p","children":"Apart from the Whop Pixel described above, Keplar does not use advertising cookies, cross-site tracking or session replay. If that ever changes, we will update this page and ask for consent where the law requires it."}]
37:["$","li","Images and video. The copy in your account stays until you delete it. The generation provider may keep its own copy for at least 7 days.",{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Images and video."}]," ","The copy in your account stays until you delete it. The generation provider may keep its own copy for at least 7 days."]}]
38:["$","li","Feedback. Kept with your account, and deleted with it.",{"children":"Feedback. Kept with your account, and deleted with it."}]
39:["$","li","Email. Messages you send us are kept as long as needed to help you.",{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Email."}]," ","Messages you send us are kept as long as needed to help you."]}]
3a:["$","p","1",{"className":"Legal-module__2dCIza__p","children":"Our database host may keep backups for a limited time after deletion. Deleted data is not restored into the product. Model providers may keep data under their own terms, as described above."}]
